{{!-- The primary menu as a tree, for the two shapes that can open a submenu: the bar and the
overlay. Called from navigation.hbs, whose context — `navigation` and `variant` — it shares.

THE CONVENTION IS IN THE LABELS. Ghost's menu is flat, so a submenu item names its parent:
"Feed / Grid" belongs to the item labelled "Feed" and displays as "Grid". A label with no " / "
is a top-level item. A buyer writes this in Settings → Navigation and nothing else.

A PARENT IS AN ITEM WHOSE NEXT ITEM IS ONE OF ITS CHILDREN. Handlebars can test one item but
cannot ask whether any item in a list matches, and a parent has to know before it draws itself —
a dropdown carries aria-expanded and a panel, a plain link does not. So the test looks one item
ahead (`from=@number limit=2` is this item and the next), and the rule a buyer follows is "put
each submenu directly under its parent". The children themselves are then collected by prefix
from anywhere in the menu. A child whose parent is missing, or whose parent is not followed by a
child, renders nowhere. A flat menu renders exactly as it did before submenus existed.

THE FRAMES ARE COUNTED, NOT GUESSED. Inside the outer loop, `../` is this partial's context.
Inside the inner loop only the SECOND iteration renders anything, and there `../../` is this
partial's context. The inner loop's first iteration is the outer item itself, the same object,
and Handlebars pushes no frame for a context that has not changed — a path read there would
resolve one level shallower than it looks, which is why nothing is read there. The last item has
no next item, so the outer loop draws it directly. --}}
{{#foreach navigation as |item|}}
	{{#match item.label "~" " / "}}{{else}}
		{{#if @last}}
			{{> "chrome/nav-item" item variant=../variant}}
		{{else}}
			{{#foreach ../navigation from=@number limit=2}}
				{{#unless @first}}
					{{#match label "~^" (concat item.label " / ")}}
						{{> "chrome/nav-group" item variant=../../variant items=../../navigation}}
					{{else}}
						{{> "chrome/nav-item" item variant=../../variant}}
					{{/match}}
				{{/unless}}
			{{/foreach}}
		{{/if}}
	{{/match}}
{{/foreach}}
